## Best Practices

### Node Management
- Always define `expected_nodes` for simulation mode
- Exclude conflicting hardware nodes explicitly
- Use critical node validation for success criteria
- Provide clear error messages for missing nodes

### Monitoring
- Use appropriate timeouts for simulation startup
- Monitor during stabilization periods
- Report progress in journal-friendly format
- Handle node failures gracefully

### Error Handling
- Validate simulator bridge existence before launch
- Provide detailed error messages for failures
- Use proper path concatenation methods
- Handle both critical and non-critical node failures

### Integration
- Integrate simulation mode with existing lifecycle management
- Provide clear command-line interface
- Maintain compatibility with existing monitoring tools
- Document simulation-specific behavior